+## Acceptance-suite defects (Voyage 1)
+
+External browser acceptance suite (Cypress) reports 5 failures. Root cause: two product defects.
+
+### Defect A — DOM identity lost on state change (4 failures)
+
+**Affected scenarios:** Marking all todos as complete, Unmarking all todos, Marking a todo as complete, Unmarking a completed todo.
+
+**Root cause:** `render()` in `js/app.js` does `dom.todoList.innerHTML = ''` then recreates every `<li>` from scratch on every state change. A real browser's Cypress holds a reference to the original `<li>` node before clicking the toggle; the node is destroyed and replaced by `render()`; the chained `.find()` / `.eq()` operates on a detached node → Cypress error.
+
+**Fix direction:** `render()` must preserve existing `<li>` nodes when their data hasn't changed. Update the existing node's classes, checkbox state, and editing state in place. Only add/remove nodes when the list composition changes. This keeps DOM identity stable across toggle interactions.
+
+**Spec added:** `specs/toggle-todo.feature:Toggling a todo preserves DOM node identity` — pins that toggling one todo must not destroy or replace sibling `<li>` nodes.
+
+### Defect B — Escape key does not discard edit (1 failure)
+
+**Affected scenario:** Discarding an edit on Escape.
+
+**Root cause:** The `blur` event listener on `.edit` input fires (capture phase) before the `keydown` Escape handler completes. Blur calls `editTodo(id, e.target.value)`, saving the current typed text to the model. Then Escape sets `editingId = null` and calls `render()`, but the model already has the new text. Result: pressing Escape saves the edit instead of discarding it.
+
+**Fix direction:** Set a flag (e.g. `escapePressed = true`) in the Escape keydown handler before the blur handler runs. In the blur handler, skip the `editTodo` call when the flag is set. Clear the flag after use.
+
+**Spec status:** `specs/edit-todo.feature:Discarding an edit on Escape` already pins correct behaviour. It will fail against the current buggy implementation. No spec change needed.
